    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d409">

                <pb facs="0492" n="388" xml:id="pg388"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/4287: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai (Cunningham) to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-19T11:00:00+08:00">February 19, 1932—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 19—3 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>75. My telegram No. 69, February 18, 3 p.m.<anchor n="65" xml:id="d409-f1"/> I
                    learn from Japanese general that last night Japanese military commander sent to
                    Chinese military commander demands for withdrawal with time limit. Press
                    agencies this morning publish demands which are similar to those told me
                    yesterday by Japanese Consul General and reported in my telegram. Japanese
                    Consulate General states news agencies reports substantially correct and one
                    translation will be ready by 3 o’clock this afternoon.</p>
                <p>Repeated to the Legation and Nanking for information.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cunningham</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
